% Test cases for the knee orthosis policy (knee_orthoses.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33318 and per payment condition of
% Policy Article A52465, each stating only what its record shows. Findings
% are recorded as the treating practitioner's or the Council's; a finding
% nobody made leaves the answer conditional. The queries: whether the claim
% is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is
% reasonable and necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base knee_orthoses cases includes these resources:
    knee_orthoses.

the knowledge base knee_orthoses cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete file for a knee orthosis with adjustable joints (L1833) for an
% ambulatory beneficiary with chronic knee instability (M23.51, group 4): the
% finding, the joint laxity tests and the examination findings in the record,
% the diagnosis on the claim line; L1833 is on the face-to-face and prior
% authorization lists, so the encounter, the order before delivery and the
% affirmed prior authorization are in the record too.
scenario adjustable_joints_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the knee orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the knee orthosis is "L1833".
    the knee orthosis is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    Ann is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "M23.51".
    the finding knee instability about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record of Ann documents the joint laxity tests performed on the knee.
    the medical record of Ann documents examination findings supporting objective joint laxity.
    claim 1 states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the knee orthosis in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the knee orthosis is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the knee orthosis is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes order date.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes description of the item.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the knee orthosis was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the knee orthosis was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the knee orthosis was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the knee orthosis.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same file without the joint laxity tests in the record: reasonable and
% necessary, but the Article's documentation of objective laxity is missing.
scenario adjustable_joints_no_laxity_tests is:
    claim 1 is for the knee orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the knee orthosis is "L1833".
    the knee orthosis is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    Ann is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "M23.51".
    the finding knee instability about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the medical record of Ann documents examination findings supporting objective joint laxity.
    claim 1 states the diagnosis code of the beneficiary.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the knee orthosis in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the knee orthosis is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the knee orthosis is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes order date.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes description of the item.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the knee orthosis includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the knee orthosis was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    prior authorization for the knee orthosis was affirmed on 2026-03-01.
    the knee orthosis was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the knee orthosis.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the medical record of Ann documents the joint laxity tests performed on the knee"]].

% An immobilizer (L1830) after knee surgery (a meniscus derangement,
% M23.211, group 2), and one for a beneficiary whose record documents no
% recent injury or surgery.
scenario immobilizer_after_surgery is:
    claim 1 is for the immobilizer.
    the HCPCS code of the immobilizer is "L1830".
    the immobilizer is furnished to Ben.
    the medical record of Ben documents recent knee surgery.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "M23.211".
    claim 2 is for the other immobilizer.
    the HCPCS code of the other immobilizer is "L1830".
    the other immobilizer is furnished to Cy.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "M23.211".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A rigid knee orthosis (L1836) for a knee flexion contracture (M24.561,
% group 1) with 25 degrees of movement, and one with 5 degrees (a fixed
% contracture): criterion fails for the second.
scenario contracture_movement is:
    claim 1 is for the rigid orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the rigid orthosis is "L1836".
    the rigid orthosis is furnished to Dee.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "M24.561".
    the movement of the knee of Dee on passive range of motion testing is 25 degrees.
    claim 2 is for the other rigid orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the other rigid orthosis is "L1836".
    the other rigid orthosis is furnished to Eve.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "M24.562".
    the movement of the knee of Eve on passive range of motion testing is 5 degrees.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A fixed contracture alone: not reasonable and necessary, at the question.
scenario fixed_contracture is:
    claim 1 is for the rigid orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the rigid orthosis is "L1836".
    the rigid orthosis is furnished to Eve.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "M24.562".
    the movement of the knee of Eve on passive range of motion testing is 5 degrees.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% An orthosis with an inflatable air bladder (L1847): no proven clinical
% benefit, never covered.
scenario air_bladder is:
    claim 1 is for the air bladder orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the air bladder orthosis is "L1847".
    the air bladder orthosis is furnished to Dee.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "M24.561".
    the movement of the knee of Dee on passive range of motion testing is 25 degrees.
    rn expects answers [].

% The osteoarthritis route of a rotation control orthosis (L1851): medial
% tibiofemoral osteoarthritis (M17.11, group 6), ambulatory, pain limiting
% function, a valgus adjustment, willing to use it; the same orthosis for a
% beneficiary who has not expressed that willingness (criterion d fails). The
% osteoarthritis codes are also in group 4: the practitioner's examination
% finds the knees stable, which closes the instability route.
scenario osteoarthritis_route is:
    claim 1 is for the unloader.
    the HCPCS code of the unloader is "L1851".
    the unloader is furnished to Fay.
    the compartment adjustment of the unloader is valgus.
    Fay is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "M17.11".
    the finding osteoarthritis limits function about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding knee instability about Fay is unsupported, according to the treating practitioner, because "the varus and valgus stress tests are negative".
    Fay expresses a willingness to use the unloader.
    claim 2 is for the other unloader.
    the HCPCS code of the other unloader is "L1851".
    the other unloader is furnished to Gus.
    the compartment adjustment of the other unloader is valgus.
    Gus is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "M17.12".
    the finding osteoarthritis limits function about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding knee instability about Gus is unsupported, according to the treating practitioner, because "the Lachman test is negative".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Additions to a covered L1852 (knee instability, M23.52): heavy duty joints
% (L2385) for a beneficiary of 320 pounds are covered; an L2405 is listed as
% not reasonable and necessary with an L1852 (no row of the table).
scenario additions is:
    claim 1 is for the heavy duty joint.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty joint is "L2385".
    the heavy duty joint is an accessory of the rotation control orthosis.
    the heavy duty joint is furnished to Hal.
    claim 2 is for the knee joint lock.
    the HCPCS code of the knee joint lock is "L2405".
    the knee joint lock is an accessory of the rotation control orthosis.
    the knee joint lock is furnished to Hal.
    the HCPCS code of the rotation control orthosis is "L1852".
    the rotation control orthosis is furnished to Hal.
    Hal is ambulatory.
    the diagnosis code of Hal is "M23.52".
    the finding knee instability about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding addition medically necessary about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Hal is 320 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The Council finds the record does not show why a prefabricated orthosis
% would not do for a custom fabricated derotation orthosis (L1840, anterior
% cruciate disruption M23.611, group 3): not reasonable and necessary.
scenario council_custom_fabrication_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the derotation orthosis.
    the HCPCS code of the derotation orthosis is "L1840".
    the derotation orthosis is furnished to Ida.
    the diagnosis code of Ida is "M23.611".
    the finding knee instability about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding custom fabrication required about Ida is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the record names no deformity, limb size or muscle mass that a prefabricated derotation orthosis could not accommodate".
    rn expects answers [].
